cate\" whether an element is a member of a subset.\n\nMore specifically, consider a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A⊆X$ is the function\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }x\\in A, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }x\\notin A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the diagram above, only the elements $-4$ and $0$ are mapped to $1.$ Therefore, the indicator function in the diagram above corresponds to the set $A=\\{-4,0\\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502110 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092338 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e380013-0002-5a17-bbf7-e9ce89e6331d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Indicator Function of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51e212d4-4747-53c2-a3de-6c59d58b03a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/45/45a423930fb07c365f10cdfbdeb3d45ef337078fa77e1b0699388088438d4c70.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501615} {:answer/id #uuid "934bef13-4408-5aeb-90a6-87735671fcd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/10/105680ffd47ba3e3a2aeb8d4b1788b521118b9759a228f049adce28323f3337b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501749} {:answer/id #uuid "9998f62b-688a-5861-b477-715c397c2226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/00/00fcd5c1eaef4303436e7abb8f5fba76aae7c83cf24a857e09130646c4f6e987.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501756} {:answer/id #uuid "d8e7f2fa-a383-5a2b-a245-5265b3274d11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/61/617f3763bcc8b674d901754934a95022327f7230c3e08d509b6818c0e87946f2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501897} {:answer/id #uuid "edf8748d-62d5-5dd2-b2cf-7abe86aa36a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/03/032816ddcb597abbd191309cbd3acf3d5356c95939cf71a334b281ba97eb5c44.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8e7f2fa-a383-5a2b-a245-5265b3274d11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/61/617f3763bcc8b674d901754934a95022327f7230c3e08d509b6818c0e87946f2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501897} :answer-field/id #uuid "5206336a-5882-5861-9285-fb57b9ddc1e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502001}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "658d443c-02c1-52f6-a2b6-cd97f500f835" :question/math-academy-id "q-174377" :question/problem "Which of the following is the indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ of the subset $A=\\{3,5\\}$ of $X=\\{1,2,3,4,5\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "An indicator function maps elements from a set to the values $0$ or $1,$ depending on whether the element belongs to a specified subset. The indicator function is designed to \"indicate\" whether an element is a member of a subset.\n\nMore specifically, consider a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A⊆X$ is the function\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }x\\in A, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }x\\notin A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe indicator function of the set $\\{3,5\\}$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/ed/ed92f46f57aefc4d9c7445f044f1b35adb89950c16f331aff35c02445b607c95.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the elements $3$ and $5$ (the elements of our subset) are mapped to $1,$ and all other elements are mapped to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409893 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd399539-33cf-5738-b970-fcc6c1d919c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Indicator Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "271bd1b2-64d9-5cc7-bbec-b86ba10fc804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453568} {:answer/id #uuid "dae1f367-953f-5742-b452-749306fe9d44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dae1f367-953f-5742-b452-749306fe9d44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453569} :answer-field/id #uuid "95b271cf-9516-5e1c-8b28-1c9dbd8c9f68" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454534} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05d4e5d4-6830-560c-878d-348a97dfcf1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453570} {:answer/id #uuid "3d8118bf-d1fb-552a-a385-b0e89891b90a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05d4e5d4-6830-560c-878d-348a97dfcf1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453570} :answer-field/id #uuid "0189df02-b3e6-5072-80bc-52efb3c878fc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454535} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9329cfe9-e21e-5113-b79d-99313f7bb970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453572} {:answer/id #uuid "d680e758-2e50-5500-9ac7-2a9c9e252fa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d680e758-2e50-5500-9ac7-2a9c9e252fa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453573} :answer-field/id #uuid "6302a2ae-7699-51e6-afdc-d665c6513e54" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454536}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8a05322-998a-5d01-8b89-68a8bc93dd0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-174380" :question/problem "Given that ${1}_{A}(0)=0,$ which of the following statements about $\\overset{―}{A}$ are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(0)=1$\n\n- **II.** ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(0)=0$\n\n- **III.** $0\\in \\overset{―}{A}$\n\n*Hint: ${1}_{A}$ denotes the indicator function of the set $A$ and ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}$ denotes the indicator function of the complement of $A.$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(0) & =1-{1}_{A}(0) \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(0)=1,$ we conclude that $0$ belongs to $\\overset{―}{A}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409888 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd399539-33cf-5738-b970-fcc6c1d919c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Indicator Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73398205-b447-5295-a67c-ad006a848004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453574} {:answer/id #uuid "66ac170a-d95d-5009-aef4-e8e0a5826587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66ac170a-d95d-5009-aef4-e8e0a5826587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453575} :answer-field/id #uuid "cabc922e-c483-5964-999a-afcbcd1b58ba" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454537} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10ebd81b-61aa-58e2-8fe6-1acf2a46536f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453576} {:answer/id #uuid "c16f5c20-ce58-58cc-a4b2-847c9c364e63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10ebd81b-61aa-58e2-8fe6-1acf2a46536f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453576} :answer-field/id #uuid "0188fa47-67f0-516d-a06e-0f6db7d50605" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454538} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31b9dc1f-cc8d-5093-ba46-67a90d725c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453578} {:answer/id #uuid "986b4a97-0064-5e3c-bb93-d96d0717fad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "986b4a97-0064-5e3c-bb93-d96d0717fad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453579} :answer-field/id #uuid "1683ca8d-d357-5b5b-a758-4c8420293a37" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09ca95e9-e7fd-5d14-80c3-ab64bc50a23d" :question/math-academy-id "q-174385" :question/problem "Given that ${1}_{A}(q)=0,$ which of the following statements about $\\overset{―}{A}$ are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(q)=1$\n\n- **II.** ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(q)=0$\n\n- **III.** $q\\in \\overset{―}{A}$\n\n*Hint: ${1}_{A}$ denotes the indicator function of the set $A$ and ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}$ denotes the indicator function of the complement of $A.$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(q) & =1-{1}_{A}(q) \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(q)=1,$ we conclude that $q$ belongs to $\\overset{―}{A}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502079 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd399539-33cf-5738-b970-fcc6c1d919c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Indicator Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "313fc3c9-7590-5457-9934-cda93c6d94c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501555} {:answer/id #uuid "4784394b-3ad7-56c7-a59a-38b9a0ea2047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501597} {:answer/id #uuid "55ddd461-5a2f-57c6-b993-62a0d935299c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501623} {:answer/id #uuid "b176ee50-07eb-571e-ad55-5d2c49c89f1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501821} {:answer/id #uuid "c216a131-75a7-5cd7-bffb-fff0f617da7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55ddd461-5a2f-57c6-b993-62a0d935299c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501623} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d770560-9db0-5560-9355-e7dc79cae0de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "221288b9-d358-51b3-a7a7-1f68c1f5fbe9" :question/math-academy-id "q-174396" :question/problem "$$\n{1}_{A}(r)=0,\\,{1}_{B}(r)=0\n$$\n\nGiven the values of the indicator functions of the sets $A$ and $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(r)=1$\n\nII. ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(r)=0$\n\nIII. $r\\in A\\cap B$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(r) & =min\\{{1}_{A}(r),{1}_{B}(r)\\} \\\\  & =min\\{0,0\\} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(r)=0,$ we conclude that $r$ does not belong to $A\\cap B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502127 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd399539-33cf-5738-b970-fcc6c1d919c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Indicator Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c956e81-ff45-5e0b-9f25-09b9d9b31488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501668} {:answer/id #uuid "736ab622-ab04-58e2-9a58-9098136b55bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501677} {:answer/id #uuid "7638f7ea-4425-5857-8b90-4445c121054f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501684} {:answer/id #uuid "f91bb51f-796c-5238-a7f9-e0d6cedfe524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501962} {:answer/id #uuid "feed8f1c-d04a-5f27-b4a6-6f25785faaa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "feed8f1c-d04a-5f27-b4a6-6f25785faaa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501971} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b452e7a-b4a9-5355-886f-bd8e112df6b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502024}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "95e868f8-4928-5f0b-9ec7-afed42df8e19" :question/math-academy-id "q-174406" :question/problem "$$\n{1}_{A}(2)=0,\\,{1}_{B}(2)=0\n$$\n\nGiven the values of the indicator functions of the sets $A$ and $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(2)=1$\n\nII. ${1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(2)=0$\n\nIII. $2\\in A\\cup B$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(2) & =max\\{{1}_{A}(2),{1}_{B}(2)\\} \\\\  & =max\\{0,0\\} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(2)=0,$ we conclude that $2$ does not belong to $A\\cup B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}]}
